       "The title 'Joothan' means food leftover by others after eating; in villages Dalits had to beg joothan from upper-caste homes — this practice, symbolising Dalit humiliation, stands at the autobiography's centre",
       "The writer was born 30 June 1950 in Barla village (Muzaffarnagar, UP) into a poor Valmiki (Chuhra) family; enduring untouchability, poverty and caste humiliation in childhood, he still gained an education",
       "The autobiography's most poignant episode — the mother throwing the joothan basket: snubbed at an upper-caste house while fetching leftovers, she carried the basket home and flung it away — 'no more begging leftovers'; this revolt is the autobiography's soul",
       "At school the writer faced untouchability — sitting apart in class, being denied water from the pitcher, teachers' scorn; yet his mother's inspiration kept his studies going",
       "Education alone is liberation's path — 'Joothan's' central message; the writer holds that only education can free Dalit society from ignorance, exploitation and humiliation",
       "'Joothan's' language is simple, sharp and truthful — everyday spoken words, rural idioms, unvarnished description; this is Dalit literature's linguistic identity",
       "Dalit literature's importance — it is the voice of the deprived; 'Joothan' confronted Hindi readers with caste system's cruel reality and gave Dalit consciousness a voice",
       "Forms of economic exploitation in the autobiography — forced labour without wages, low wages, work in exchange for leftovers, the debt trap; social exploitation — untouchability, temple-entry bans, separate wells",
       "The writer's mother is the autobiography's heroine — a blend of patience and revolt; she never surrendered self-respect even in poverty; her character symbolises Dalit woman-power",
       "Valmiki's other works — 'Salaam' (story collection), 'Ghuspaithiye' (poetry collection); he remained a leading voice of the Dalit literary movement",
       "'Joothan's' universal message — human dignity, self-respect and equality; it is not only Dalits' tale but the saga of every humiliated human's struggle",
       "Word meanings: 'जूठन' = बचा-खुचा भोजन; 'छुआछूत' = जाति के नाम पर भेदभाव; 'सामंती' = शोषक व्यवस्था वाला; 'वेदना' = पीड़ा; 'हाशिए' = किनारे/उपेक्षित वर्ग; 'प्रामाणिकता' = सच्चा/विश्वसनीय होना; 'स्वाभिमान' = आत्म-सम्मान; 'यथार्थ' = वास्तविकता; 'दलित' = दबा-कुचला वर्ग; 'विद्रोह' = विरोध/बगावत।"
