       "Barahmasa is the famous convention of separation-poetry — the heroine's sorrow is described through the twelve months' changing nature; Nagmati's lament is its finest example",
       "In Sufi philosophy love itself is the path of discipline — through the worldly love-tale (Ratnasen-Padmavati) Jayasi hints at transcendental love (the soul's union with the Supreme); this is the essence of the prem-margi branch",
       "For Jayasi, separation is love's touchstone — love is purified in viraha's fire; Nagmati's viraha is this philosophy in poetic form",
       "The Kadwak's language is chaste Awadhi — Jayasi enlivened it with folk idioms, proverbs and rural imagery; Persian-Arabic words too occur naturally",
       "Jayasi's style is influenced by the Masnavi manner — he wedded the Persian Masnavi tale-poem tradition to the Indian premakhyana tradition",
