       "Nabhadas is Bhaktikal's famous saint-poet — of the Ramanandi tradition, disciple of his guru Agradas; Tulsidas's contemporary; his immortal 'Bhaktamal' portrays about 200 devotees' lives in Chhappay metre",
       "'Bhaktamal' is called Bhaktikal's 'history' — it gathers the life-sketches of devotees like Kabir, Surdas, Tulsidas, Mira, Namdev; Acharya Ramchandra Shukla drew richly on Bhaktamal while writing Hindi literature's history",
       "Nabhadas sang the devotees' glory in 'Bhaktamal' — his aim was to present the devotees' sacrifice, love and fidelity as ideals; famous sayings like 'Sur Sur Tulsi Sasi' are Bhaktamal's own gift",
       "Chhappay is a six-foot metre — made of four Rolas (24 morae each) + two Ullalas; eminently suited to descriptive and eulogistic themes; Nabhadas chose this very metre for the devotee-sketches",
       "'Bhaktamal' is a compendium — blending history and devotion; the devotees' sketches are brief, pithy and inspiring in style; Priyadas wrote the 'Bhaktirasabodhini' commentary on it",
       "Nabhadas's vision is all-seeing — he gave equal reverent place to nirguna-saguna, Shaiva-Vaishnava, men and women devotees; devotees like Mira and Namdev and women saints too are portrayed honourably",
       "Nabhadas belongs to the Ramanandi tradition — Ramananda made the Bhakti movement a people's movement in north India; opposing caste, he initiated disciples like Kabir and Raidas; Nabhadas is this tradition's bearer",
       "The Chhappays' tongue is mixed Brajbhasha — simple, flowing and emotional; ornaments occur effortlessly; the Guru's glory and the devotee's glory shine in every Chhappay",
       "Nabhadas is called 'Bhaktikal's historian' — without him many Bhaktikal poets' introductions would stay incomplete; reading Bhaktamal gives the Bhakti movement's whole picture",
       "The textbook Chhappays' chief theme is bhakti's glory — the true devotee is one who, quitting ego, is rapt in love, service and surrender; sacrifice and renunciation dominate the Chhappays",
       "The Bhakti movement's social side was vital — devotees opposed caste discrimination, preached in people's tongues and gave society moral strength; Nabhadas enshrined this consciousness in his text",
       "The Chhappays' message stays relevant today — devotion, humility, love and people's welfare aid students' character-building; by brevity's art, great feelings fit in a small metre",
       "Word meanings: 'छप्पय' = छह चरणों का छंद; 'रोला' = छप्पय का एक अंग; 'उल्लाला' = छप्पय का एक अंग; 'महिमा' = बड़ाई; 'श्रद्धा' = आदरपूर्ण विश्वास; 'त्याग' = छोड़ना/समर्पण; 'ईश्वरनिष्ठा' = ईश्वर में दृढ़ विश्वास; 'संत-कवि' = संत और कवि; 'संग्रह' = संकलन; 'प्रशस्ति' = गुणगान।"
