       "It was published in 1820 in the volume 'Lamia, Isabella, The Eve of St Agnes, and Other Poems'.",
       "Keats trained as an apothecary-surgeon before leaving medicine for poetry — his sense of the physical world is exact.",
       "Each ode stanza has 11 lines in iambic pentameter — a stanza-form Keats invented for this poem.",
       "Key lines — 'Where are the songs of spring? Ay, where are they? / Think not of them, thou hast thy music too' — the poem's turning point.",
